\noindent Where $H(X) = -\sum_X P(X) \log P(X)$; Here and throughout
the paper we use natural logarithms, so the entropy is measured in
{\it NATS}, and also adopt the convention $0 \log 0 \equiv 0$.

We define the following functions : \begin{equation}
F_N(M,T,[\epsilon]_1^{N}) = H([Z]_1^N) - H([Z]_1^{N-1}) \end{equation}

\noindent Setting all the $\epsilon_i$'s equal, reduces us back to the $Y$
process, so in particular $F_N(M,T, (\epsilon,\ldots,\epsilon)) =
C_N(\epsilon)$.

\noindent $C_N^{(k)}$ is obtained by summing $F_N^{\vec{k}}$ on all
$\vec{k}$'s with weight $k$ : \begin{equation} C_N^{(k)} =
\sum_{\vec{k},\omega(\vec{k})=k} F_N^{\vec{k}} \end{equation}
